            "description": "health_probe_port is the port for a separate PLAINTEXT gRPC listener that\n serves ONLY grpc.health.v1. k8s kubelet probes are plaintext-only and\n cannot speak TLS, so the main TLS port (listen_address) is invisible to\n them. This listener runs on a completely separate grpc.Server / tonic\n Server / NettyServerBuilder with no TLS, no auth interceptors, and no\n business services registered — isolation is the security argument.\n The health status reflects the same StatusSink-driven state as the TLS\n health endpoint: NOT_SERVING until bootstrap completes, then tracks\n handler health (UNHEALTHY → NOT_SERVING, recovery → SERVING).\n Default: 8444. Set to 0 to disable the plaintext health probe listener.",
            "default": 8444
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "cred_pair_id",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "cred_pair_id is the id of the cluster cred_pair this invocation\n authenticates as. Used as the `kid` header in the signed JWT\n presented to kernel.Mint.MintClientToken. Must match one of\n kernel.Config.root_cred_pairs[*].id on the target cluster.",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 128 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 128,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "format",
      "type": "enum",
      "description": "format is the default output format for command results (tenant\n listings, etc.). Overridable per-invocation via --format. Default\n is JSON for machine consumption (cavalierctl is CI-first).",
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_enum_defined",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "enum_values": [
        {
          "name": "OUTPUT_FORMAT_JSON",
          "number": 1,
          "description": "JSON format"
        },
        {
          "name": "OUTPUT_FORMAT_YAML",
          "number": 2,
          "description": "YAML format"
        },
        {
          "name": "OUTPUT_FORMAT_MULTI_YAML",
          "number": 3,
          "description": "Multi YAML format (e.g. ---)"
        },
        {
          "name": "OUTPUT_FORMAT_TEXT",
          "number": 4,
          "description": "Plain text format"
        },
        {
          "name": "OUTPUT_FORMAT_ENV_VAR",
          "number": 5,
          "description": "Environment variable format"
        },
        {
          "name": "OUTPUT_FORMAT_PROTO_WIRE",
          "number": 6,
          "description": "Protobuf wire format (binary)"
        },
        {
          "name": "OUTPUT_FORMAT_TOML",
          "number": 7,
          "description": "TOML format"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "trace_id",
      "type": "string",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "default_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 32768,
          "defaulted": true,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "default_bound"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "noop",
      "type": "bool"
    }
  ]
}

fields.description:
InitialFields is a map of fields to include in every log entry
 Useful for adding context like service name, version, environment, etc.
 Example: {"service": "api", "version": "1.0.0", "environment": "production"}

types.schema_json:
{
  "name": "CredPair",
  "package": "credentials",
  "description": "CredPair is a tenant-scoped credential. Public key stored in the tenant's\n KernelTenantConfig slice; private key never leaves the holder. Used to\n authenticate kernel.TenantAdmin RPCs and (downstream) any tenant-scoped\n RPC across the cluster.\n\n A request authenticated by CredPair carries the SPIFFE URI\n `spiffe://\u003cspiffe_prefix\u003e/\u003ctenant_name\u003e/users/cred-pair:\u003cid\u003e`.\n\n `entitlements` must always be a subset of the tenant's ceiling\n (kernel.Constraints.entitlements_ceiling). Enforcement is in\n kernel.TenantAdmin.SetTenantConfig.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "id",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "id is a unique identifier for this cred_pair within its owning tenant.",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "minimum size: 1",
        "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_min_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 1,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "default_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 32768,
          "defaulted": true,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "default_bound"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "tenant_name",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "tenant_name names the owning tenant — the namespace that `namespaces` are\n relative to. The cluster cred_pair's owner is the root \"/\".",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "default_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 32768,
          "defaulted": true,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "default_bound"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "public_key",
      "type": "message",
      "description": "public_key is the cred_pair's public key, as a JWK. Mint verifies a\n cred_pair-signed proof against it to issue a token.",
      "required": true,
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "message": {
        "name": "Jwk",
        "package": "jwk",
        "description": "Jwk represents a JSON Web Key as defined in RFC 7517.\n It contains the public key parameters for RSA (e, n), EC (crv, x, y), or OKP (crv, x) keys.\n JWK is used for key distribution and verification in JSON-based protocols like JWT.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "kty",
            "type": "enum",
            "description": "Kty is the key type parameter (RSA, EC, or OKP)",
            "enum_values": [
              {
                "name": "KEY_TYPE_RSA",
                "number": 1,
                "description": "KeyTypeRsa represents an RSA key type"
              },
              {
                "name": "KEY_TYPE_EC",
                "number": 2,
                "description": "KeyTypeEc represents an Elliptic Curve key type"
              },
              {
                "name": "KEY_TYPE_OKP",
                "number": 3,
                "description": "KeyTypeOkp represents an Octet Key Pair (EdDSA) key type"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "alg",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Alg is the algorithm intended for use with the key (e.g., \"RS384\", \"ES256\", \"EdDSA\")",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 64 bytes",
              "minimum size: 1"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 64,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_min_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "kid",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Kid is the key ID used to match keys with signatures",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 512 bytes",
              "minimum size: 1"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 512,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_min_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "use",
            "type": "enum",
            "description": "Use indicates the intended use of the key (sig for signatures, enc for encryption)",
            "enum_values": [
              {
                "name": "JWK_USE_TYPE_SIG",
                "number": 1,
                "description": "JwkUseTypeSig indicates the key is used for digital signatures"
              },
              {
                "name": "JWK_USE_TYPE_ENC",
                "number": 2,
                "description": "JwkUseTypeEnc indicates the key is used for encryption"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "e",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "E is the RSA public exponent (base64url encoded without padding)",
            "constraints": [
              "must be base64 encoded",
              "maximum size: 64 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 64,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_base64",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "n",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "N is the RSA modulus (base64url encoded without padding)",
            "constraints": [
              "must be base64 encoded",
              "maximum size: 1024 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1024,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_base64",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "crv",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Crv is the elliptic curve name (e.g., P-256, P-384, P-521, Ed25519)",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 64 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 64,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "x",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "X is the x coordinate for EC keys or the public key for OKP (base64url encoded without padding)",
            "constraints": [
              "must be base64 encoded",
              "maximum size: 256 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 256,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_base64",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "y",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Y is the y coordinate for EC keys (base64url encoded without padding, not used for OKP)",
            "constraints": [
              "must be base64 encoded",
              "maximum size: 256 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 256,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_base64",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "exp",
            "type": "int64",
            "description": "Exp is the expiration in epoch seconds. This is not part of the JWK spec as the spec does\n not specify how to handle public key expiration.\n When stored in a collection with epoch_expiration, the state store computes TTL = exp - now\n and auto-evicts the entry on expiry."
          },
          {
            "name": "created",
            "type": "int64",
            "description": "Created is the Unix epoch timestamp (seconds) when the key was created (optional).\n If set, valid range: 1735689600 (2025-01-01) to 8045740800 (2225-01-01)",
            "constraints": [
              "must be \u003e= 1735689600",
              "must be \u003c= 8045740800"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_ge",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1735689600,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_le",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 8045740800,
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "entitlements",
      "type": "message",
      "description": "entitlements this cred_pair holds (⊆ the owning tenant's ceiling), as the\n SAME TokenEntitlements the C2S authorizer checks: the minted cred_pair token\n sets service_entitlements = this directly (uniform with IDP-user tokens).",
      "message": {
        "name": "TokenEntitlements",
        "package": "entitlements",
        "description": "TokenEntitlements holds compressed C2S entitlements embedded in user tokens.\n OPA returns this structure directly; the token authority embeds it in the JWT service_entitlements claim.\n grants may contain exact or wildcard grant tokens; generated helpers normalize them before authorization.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "grants",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "grants is a flat list of generated grant tokens, e.g. PACKAGE_SERVICE_RPC.",
            "repeated": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 1024 elements (default)",
              "maximum element size: 32768 bytes (default)"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "default_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1024,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "elements",
                "source": "default_bound"
              },
              {
                "rule": "default_max_element_size",
                "target": "element",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 32768,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "default_bound"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "data_grants",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "data_grants is a flat list of generated data-entitlement grant tokens, e.g.\n PACKAGE_RECORD_FIELD. A data grant names what the caller may SEE RAW: a MAY_*\n redact field with a matching grant egresses raw; absent a grant the field gets\n its most-protective default (MAY_REDACT -\u003e REDACT, MAY_ANONYMIZE -\u003e ANONYMIZE).\n Stamped by OPA at token-exchange time alongside grants — an identity property,\n never a request parameter.",
            "repeated": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 1024 elements (default)",
              "maximum element size: 32768 bytes (default)"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "default_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1024,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "elements",
                "source": "default_bound"
              },
              {
                "rule": "default_max_element_size",
                "target": "element",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 32768,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "default_bound"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "azp",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "azp restricts these entitlements to tokens with a matching authorized party.\n Empty = entitlements apply regardless of azp.",
            "repeated": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 1024 elements (default)",
              "maximum element size: 32768 bytes (default)"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "default_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1024,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "elements",
                "source": "default_bound"
              },
              {
                "rule": "default_max_element_size",
                "target": "element",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 32768,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "default_bound"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "namespaces",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "namespaces are the authorized namespaces, RELATIVE to the owning tenant\n (e.g. \"default\", \"prod\", or \"*\" for all of the tenant's projects). The\n cred_pair can only act at-or-below these and literally cannot name another\n tenant. The cluster cred_pair is relative to \"/\", so it can span tenants.",
      "repeated": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 256 elements",
        "maximum element size: 32768 bytes (default)"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 256,
          "unit": "elements",
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "default_max_element_size",
          "target": "element",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 32768,
          "defaulted": true,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "default_bound"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "description",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "description is a human-readable label.",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 256 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 256,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "created_at",
      "type": "message",
      "description": "created_at is when this credential was created."
    },
    {
      "name": "expires_at",
      "type": "message",
      "description": "expires_at is the optional expiry. Zero value means no expiry."
    },
    {
      "name": "trace_id",
      "type": "string",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "default_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 32768,
          "defaulted": true,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "default_bound"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "noop",
      "type": "bool"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Entitlements",
  "package": "credentials",
  "description": "Entitlements is a set of SPIFFE URI grants. Each grant is a pattern that\n may contain `*` wildcards on path segments. An action against a resource\n is permitted if the resource's SPIFFE URI matches any grant.\n\n Example grants:\n   spiffe://local/dev/_cluster/services/sentinel   — full sentinel access\n   spiffe://local/dev/_cluster/services/argus/*    — any argus RPC\n   spiffe://local/dev/_models/anthropic/claude-*   — LLM model scoping\n\n A tenant's own subtree (spiffe://\u003cprefix\u003e/\u003ctenant_name\u003e/...) is implicitly\n granted to all principals inside that tenant and need not be listed.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "grants",
