{
  "name": "GraphTypeAnnotation",
  "package": "spec",
  "description": "GraphTypeAnnotation marks a proto message as a graph type for schema generation.\n Used to generate mutation handlers and graph store projections.\n\n Design decisions (D1, D2, D3 from the graph schema plan):\n\n D1: Annotations go on SOURCE messages (e.g. GraphEntity in aegis.proto),\n not on the consumer. The source messages are the authority on the data model.\n This follows the same pattern as service_state, topic, and subscribe —\n the annotation lives where the structure is defined.\n\n D2: Nested messages WITHOUT graph_type are serialized as JSON string\n predicates. Graph storage is for traversal (structural fields), not\n analytical queries on metadata. JSON storage avoids ~50 null predicates\n per entity, prevents schema churn, and allows incremental promotion.\n\n D3: xid_field controls the mutation strategy. When set, subscribe-gen\n generates a conditional upsert by external id (xid) — query by xid,\n then update-or-insert. When empty, subscribe-gen generates JSON insert (append-only).",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "name",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "name is the graph type name (e.g. \"Entity\", \"Edge\").",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
